    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2011-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The remainder when \\(2011\\) is divided by \\(60\\) is \\(31.\\) This means that \\(2011 = 60 \\cdot 33 + 31,\\) which means that \\(2011\\) minutes is the same as \\(33\\) hours and \\(31\\) minutes.\n\n\\(24\\) hours takes us to January \\(2,\\) so we get that we are \\(9\\) hours and \\(31\\) minutes into January \\(2.\\)\n\nThus, D is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "After the first \\(24\\) hours, the remaining time is on January \\(2.\\)",
        "Divide \\(2011\\) minutes by \\(60\\)."
      ],
